@startuml
title Use Cases - Redis-like Server
left to right direction

actor Client
actor Operator

rectangle "Redis-like Server" {
  usecase "Connect over TCP\n(RESP or inline)" as UC5
  usecase "Store and read data\n(strings, lists, hashes, sets)" as UC1
  usecase "Expire keys\n(SET EX/PX, TTL, PERSIST)" as UC2
  usecase "Inspect the keyspace\n(KEYS, TYPE, EXISTS, DBSIZE)" as UC3
  usecase "Snapshot data to disk\n(SAVE, BGSAVE)" as UC6
  usecase "Rewrite the append-only file\n(BGREWRITEAOF)" as UC8
  usecase "Inspect the server\n(INFO, CONFIG GET)" as UC4
  usecase "Change the log level\n(CONFIG SET loglevel)" as UC10
  usecase "Configure the server\n(options, config file, environment)" as UC7
  usecase "Stop the server\n(SIGTERM: final save)" as UC11
  usecase "Watch the logs\n(watchdog warnings, crash reports)" as UC12
  usecase "Extend system features" as UC9
}

Client --> UC5
Client --> UC1
Client --> UC2
Client --> UC3
Client --> UC6
Client --> UC8
Client --> UC4
Client --> UC10

Operator --> UC7
Operator --> UC11
Operator --> UC12
Operator --> UC9

UC1 <.. UC2 : <<extend>>
UC1 ..> UC8 : write commands\nare logged

note right of UC10
  Only with --enable-config-set:
  there is no authentication.
end note

note right of UC9
  BR-009: for future features
  such as Pub/Sub
end note

@enduml
